{
 "encounter_id": "00864",
 "speakers": {
  "person_1": "PATIENT",
  "person_2": "DOCTOR"
 },
 "turns": [
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Athlete's foot. Between the toes. It's back."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "How long has it been there this time?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Dunno. A while. Weeks."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Which foot?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Both. Worse on the left. Itchy. Skin's peeling."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Have you tried anything?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Clotrimazole cream. Twice a day. And a powder in my shoes."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "How long did you use the cream for? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "A week. It went. Then it came back. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "How long should you use it for? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Dunno. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Usually another week or two after it looks better. That's why it comes back. Any health conditions?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Diabetes. Type 2."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Anyone in the family get fungal infections?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "My dad had it on his nails."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any fever, or redness spreading up the foot?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No. Nothing like that."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any pain, or numbness in your feet?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No. Normal."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Pulse and temperature, please. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Okay. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Pulse 74, temperature 36.7.",
   "pause": 10.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Fine? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Fine. Take your socks off and let me see.",
   "pause": 18.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Here. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "There's white, peeling, soggy skin between the little toes on both feet, and a small crack on the left, but no redness spreading, and no sign of infection. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "What is it? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "It's the same fungal infection, athlete's foot, tinea pedis, and I'd say it's recurrent because the treatment was stopped too soon, or the shoes are keeping the feet damp."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "What do I do? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Continue the clotrimazole cream for two weeks after it looks clear, and dry between your toes thoroughly after washing."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Right. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Wear cotton socks, change them daily, and alternate your shoes. Don't go barefoot in communal showers."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Okay. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And I'd like to take a skin scraping, to confirm the diagnosis, because it's come back."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Fine.",
   "pause": 10.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Done. Because you have diabetes, check your feet daily and see me if there's a blister, a crack that won't heal, or redness."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Okay. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I'd like to see you again in three weeks, with the result."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Three weeks. Thanks. ~"
  }
 ],
